# Attachment upload = encrypt.lu single PUT (chunking temporary)

encrypt.lu proves Safari can PUT ~22 MiB in one XHR when the hop is equivalent.
Do **not** treat “Safari needs 1 MiB chunks” as the main story. Find the delta.

## Primary recipe (always on — do not “secure away”)

| Requirement | Value |
|---|---|
| Page | `https://privatenote.ai` (not `*.pages.dev`) |
| Upload | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` |
| Transport | Safari **XHR** only for the body (Chrome uses the same XHR single-PUT path) |
| Body | one untyped Blob |
| Method | PUT `/api/notes/:id/file` |
| Auth | **Bearer first**, then **query-token fallback** (required for WebKit) |
| Cookies | off (`credentials: "omit"`) |
| Proxy | never Pages `/api` for the binary body |

**Do not remove query-token fallback** to “improve security.” Bearer is preferred (token stays out of URLs); query is the proven Safari recovery path. Harden around it instead: redact tokens in logs, shrink post-upload finalize TTL, clear reservation on note create, reject hash mismatches (409).

A/B: same Mac Safari, same ~22 MiB file — encrypt.lu one PUT 200, then privatenote.ai → upload.privatenote.ai. If prod same-site still aborts in ~200 ms with no Worker log, bug is CF/Worker on the upload host (Bot Fight, WAF, Access, rate limit), not the encrypt algorithm.

## CORS (upload relay)

Match `relay.encrypt.lu`: echo Origin, Allow-Headers echo (authorization), Allow-Methods GET/POST/PUT/OPTIONS, Max-Age 86400, **no** Allow-Credentials.

## Temporary chunking

`SAFARI_CHUNKING_ENABLED` defaults **false**. Re-enable only after prod same-site single PUT fails and CF/CORS deltas are ruled out. Then: few ~4 MiB serial PUTs — not many 1 MiB POSTs.
